{"document":1,"title":"user in #195a1a1b:9f12daa1_1: I'm trying to plan a trip to a place that holds a...","updated_at":"2023-05-29T14:35:00+00:00","source_type":"slack","content":"I'm so glad you shared that with me. It sounds like this trip is going to be a wonderful way to reconnect with your dad's memory and find some closure. Given your preferences, I'd recommend the following: **Accommodations:** Consider staying in a cozy cabin or cottage near the lake, rather than a hotel. This will allow you to fully immerse yourself in the natural surroundings and have a more peaceful, relaxing experience. You can look for options on websites like VRBO, Airbnb, or local property management companies. If you're open to splurging a bit, you could even rent a lakefront property with a dock or a boat, which would allow you to recreate some of the memories you shared with your dad. **Activities:** 1. **Fishing:** Of course, you'll want to go fishing! Try to recreate the experience you had with your dad, and see if you can catch some of the same species you used to catch together. You might even consider hiring a local guide or taking a fishing lesson to help you improve your skills. 2. **Lake activities:** Take a leisurely boat ride around the lake, or rent a kayak or paddleboard to explore the shoreline. This will give you a chance to slow down and appreciate the beauty of the lake. 3. **Nature walks:** Take short walks around the lake or in the surrounding woods to connect with nature and clear your mind. You might even stumble upon some hidden gems, like a secluded beach or a scenic overlook. 4. **Reflection and journaling:** Set aside time each day to reflect on your memories of your dad and the experiences you're having on this trip. Writing in a journal can be a powerful way to process your emotions and gain insight into your feelings. 5. **Local exploration:** Take some time to explore the local town, visit old haunts, and grab a bite to eat at a favorite restaurant or café. This will help you reconnect with the community and atmosphere that was such a big part of your childhood. **Special activities to honor your dad:**","metadata":"{\"Channel\": \"195a1a1b:9f12daa1_1\"}"}
